Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the *Software Engineer I* position with *Acrisure*. I bring more than four years of professional software engineering experience building backend APIs, workflow platforms, integrations, and production tooling, along with a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University.

At Sperse, I build and maintain APIs, workflows, integrations, and tooling for a multi-agent CRM platform using Python, FastAPI, LangGraph, and LangChain. The system routes requests across 40+ specialized sub-agents with secure access control for more than 10,000 users. I also developed a JavaScript/TypeScript and React Flow workflow platform with durable Temporal execution and Redis progress tracking, created a FastMCP integration that exposes 160+ backend actions as safe, validated tool calls, and implemented GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines with automated OpenTelemetry testing. That combination of modular API development, testing, debugging, monitoring, and operational support directly matches Acrisure's need for an engineer who can deliver defined work with quality while contributing to production systems.

My earlier work at Qualitest strengthened the integration and operational judgment I would bring to Acrisure's policy administration platform. I built a Java and Spring Boot Storage Service API backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, standardizing uploads, downloads, deletions, and expiring signed URLs across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I also debugged and optimized PostgreSQL queries and automated long-running production workflows with AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda, improving error recovery and supporting more than 100K weekly executions. These projects required structured problem solving, clear collaboration with business stakeholders, and ownership of reliable workflows—the same habits Acrisure emphasizes through accountability, candid communication, and delivering for clients.

I am especially drawn to Acrisure's mission to help people and businesses grow and protect what matters most by combining human expertise with advanced technology. My AI-assisted engineering experience—including an OpenAI Codex code-review integration that automates PR triage across 25–30 pull requests per week—would help me learn the insurance domain quickly and contribute practical improvements to developer workflows, testing, and documentation. I would welcome the opportunity to support Acrisure's underwriting and policy administration teams while growing within a culture that wins together and turns challenges into possibilities.

I would love to discuss my interest in this position with your team and can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to connecting!

